ok - executing fm-jev-lib.sh is refused; it is sourceable only
ok - with only OPENROUTER_API_KEY, decide uses the OpenRouter URL and bearer header
ok - with only TYPESAFE_API_KEY, decide uses the TypeSafe URL and bearer header
ok - fm_jev_decide keeps auto-detection for existing callers
ok - with both keys and no JEV_ROUTE, TypeSafe wins
ok - JEV_ROUTE=openrouter selects OpenRouter even when a TypeSafe key is present
ok - JEV_MODEL overrides the route default
ok - JEV_MODEL warns on unpinned overrides while honoring them
ok - JEV_URL is a complete POST URL used verbatim
ok - JEV_BASE keeps default path building from the origin
ok - JEV_URL wins over JEV_BASE
ok - OpenRouter ignores JEV_BASE so /v1/systemone is never appended
ok - timeout defaults to 25s and JEV_TIMEOUT overrides it
ok - .env supplies URL, model, and timeout; the environment wins
ok - OPENROUTER_API_KEY in .env activates the OpenRouter route
ok - environment TYPESAFE_API_KEY wins over .env
ok - key configuration is a presence gate independent of route resolution
ok - absent keys fail closed without a network call
ok - questions that are not a JSON object fail before curl
ok - a non-200 response is a hard failure with no stdout JSON
ok - a curl transport failure is a hard failure
ok - missing curl is a usage failure
ok - choice confidence floor defaults to 0.7 and accepts an explicit dispatch-style 0.6
ok - probabilities must be 0..1 numbers that sum to about 1
ok - shared privacy screen preserves every benign fixture and blocks every sensitive fixture
ok - compact-state strips obvious secrets and refuses oversized input
ok - log helper writes one JSONL line and keeps secrets out of it
ok - response-model helper names the exact build that answered
ok - log helper defaults to $FM_HOME/state/jev-calls.jsonl
